WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.940
A federal judge rejected Trump officials bid to set aside California ballots, with no immediate action ordered. This is Omni View North America, Episode 31. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. Ontario is set to name regional chairs by appointment. Automakers say parts and fuel are costing more, and NVIDIA's chief is tied to a spy report out of Beijing. The New York Times calls the California ruling another setback as the administration moves to target voting by non-citizens.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:32.620
The court left those ballots in place because it found no immediate action was required.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.240
That is a court result, not a new statute.

00:00:36.423 --> 00:00:39.243
Ontario will appoint hand-picked regional chairs within weeks.

00:00:39.903 --> 00:00:43.703
CBC says the province is choosing them, rather than leaving the choice to voters.

00:00:44.323 --> 00:00:45.723
Critics call that undemocratic.

00:00:46.263 --> 00:00:47.463
The objection is the method.

00:00:48.003 --> 00:00:51.883
Chairs picked by hand, installed by appointment, on a clock measured in weeks.

00:00:52.423 --> 00:00:56.923
The report is an announcement of what the province will do, not a list of chairs already named.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:01:04.267
American auto companies say they are paying more for computer chips, steel and copper, and for the fuel that moves their products.

00:01:04.747 --> 00:01:08.587
NPR puts tariffs, diesel, and computer chips at the center of that rise.

00:01:09.107 --> 00:01:13.827
The companies are talking about parts inside the vehicles, and about the fuel that carries finished cars.

00:01:14.347 --> 00:01:18.747
What NPR has is the company's account of higher bills, not a published price index.

00:01:19.852 --> 00:01:24.872
The New York Times says Nvidia Chief Jensen Huang is seen as the target of a Chinese spy plot.

00:01:24.872 --> 00:01:29.972
A Chinese businesswoman who had a close relationship with Huang was found to be passing intelligence

00:01:29.972 --> 00:01:30.532
to Beijing.

00:01:31.172 --> 00:01:33.512
President Trump was briefed and took no action.

00:01:34.072 --> 00:01:37.872
The paper's account is that the intelligence went to Beijing from someone close to Huang

00:01:38.182 --> 00:01:40.752
and that the president once told did not act.

00:01:41.787 --> 00:01:46.387
The Guardian says a handful of college students made jokes about Pat McAfee online before

00:01:46.387 --> 00:01:48.947
his college game day stop at the University of Utah.

00:01:49.427 --> 00:01:50.927
He hosts the Pat McAfee show.

00:01:50.927 --> 00:01:57.447
The paper says he landed a five-year, $85 million deal in 2023 to take that show to ESPN.

00:01:58.047 --> 00:02:01.467
It says his presence on college game day helped push ratings to new heights.

00:02:02.107 --> 00:02:08.627
ESPN executives were reportedly in talks on a new contract worth between $60 million and $65 million a year.

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:13.567
One executive, the Guardian says, described him as a generational media talent.

00:02:13.947 --> 00:02:17.887
The outlet's own words cast him as the star of an ESPN era of stunts

00:02:17.887 --> 00:02:23.367
and what it calls meme brain swill." That is the paper talking, not a label McAfee has taken up.

00:02:23.807 --> 00:02:26.627
The Guardian says the weekend then went wrong, in its telling.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:29.247
Students at Utah posted ahead of the appearance.

00:02:29.787 --> 00:02:33.247
The writer says it tacked is too strong. They made a few mild jokes.

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:36.927
McAfee's first reaction, which the paper quotes, was this.

00:02:37.487 --> 00:02:41.747
The university's Instagram account posted something talking a little trash about me last night,

00:02:41.987 --> 00:02:46.167
which I certainly love. He said that ahead of the youth's game against the Houston Cougars.

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:50.847
The Guardian's writer argues the reaction shows someone happy to whip a crowd into a hostile

00:02:50.847 --> 00:02:52.967
frenzy and terrified of criticism.

00:02:53.527 --> 00:02:57.767
The piece does not report a canceled stop, a dropped contract, or a ratings figure

00:02:57.767 --> 00:02:58.287
for Utah.

00:02:58.787 --> 00:03:03.907
What it does put on the page is the 2023 deal, the reported yearly range, the generational

00:03:03.907 --> 00:03:08.187
line, the students' jokes, and McAfee's remark before Utah played Houston.

